ft changelog

2026-08-27
  - Fix: Memory leak, ~12.8 MB per closed tab or split pane.
    terminal_free() freed the screen and alternate screen but never the
    scrollback history, which is HISTSIZE (10000) lines allocated up front
    per terminal. A session that opened and closed tabs grew without bound.
  - Fix: Two libpng error paths leaked. bgimg_load() and xseticonpng()
    freed only the row pointer array, not the rows themselves, when libpng
    longjmped out on a broken file. The locals read after the jump were
    also not volatile, so their values there were not guaranteed.
  - Fix: drawutf8string() leaked the fallback FcPattern when
    XftFontOpenPattern() failed. On success the font takes ownership; on
    failure the caller still has to destroy it.

2026-08-26
  - Fix: Scroll-select. Dragging a selection past the top/bottom edge of a
    pane now keeps scrolling while the button is held, instead of only
    advancing one line per mouse-motion event (holding the pointer still
    outside the pane stopped the scrolling altogether). Driven from the main
    loop, tunable via autoscrolllines/autoscrolldelay in config.h.
  - Fix: Scroll-select downwards no longer loses its anchor. selscrolldown()
    clamped the selection origin to row 0, so once the origin scrolled above
    the viewport the selection silently started at the wrong line. The origin
    may now sit outside the viewport; TLINE()/tlinelen()/selnormalize()
    resolve and clamp it against the history buffer.
  - Fix: Selection was dropped or drifted when output arrived while viewing
    scrollback. The viewport stays pinned to the same history content there,
    so tscrollup() no longer also shifts the selection.
  - Fix: A press-drag-release starting in an unfocused pane selects text
    instead of only changing focus. The click is still swallowed when the
    newly focused pane runs a mouse-aware app (e.g. nvim). Focusing another
    pane now also clears the previous pane's highlight.

2026-02-07
  - Feature: Background image support. Display a PNG image behind terminal
    text with configurable transparency using XRender compositing. The image
    uses fill/crop scaling and rescales on window resize. Controlled via Lua
    API: st.set_background_image(), st.set_background_opacity(),
    st.get_background_image(), st.get_background_opacity().

2026-02-06
  - Fix: Crash when scrolling up after window maximize. History buffer
    columns were not initialized after resize, causing garbage data to be
    passed to libXft font rendering (segfault in libXft.so).
  - Fix: Word/line selection (double/triple click) now works correctly when
    scrolled into history. selsnap() was using term.line instead of TLINE().
  - Fix: Cursor blink freezing during tty activity. The blink toggle was
    being skipped when output arrived within the latency window.
